ded labels placed from OpenStreetMap, Horry County and Census coordinates.</div><div role="listitem">Houses on streets that end in cul-de-sacs in Carolina Forest, with woods around them and land being cleared for more on the right. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>.</div><div role="listitem">The Market Common from the air: its homes, outlined, Valor Park and Grand Park beside the shops. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from one NOAA aerial photo, resized it, adjusted the colors and added an outline and labels.</div><div role="listitem">The old Socastee swing bridge, the blue steel span, on the Intracoastal Waterway, with the newer highway bridge at the lower left. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>.</div><div role="listitem">The Surfside Beach pier from the air, with the beach parking lots and the streets of beach houses behind it. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from one NOAA aerial photo, resized it, adjusted the colors and added a label.</div><div role="listitem">Beach houses at Garden City, seen from over the ocean, with the salt marsh and its creeks behind them. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Houses on the creek side of Business 17 in Murrells Inlet, with docks reaching out over the marsh edge to the creek. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service and added labels placed from map data.</div><div role="listitem">The north end of Pawleys Island at low tide: houses along the dune line, and the inlet at right. Photo: Phoebe, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pawleys_Island_North_End.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Resized and saved as WebP by Chapter3 Realty; the file is not cut. The page crops it with the browser.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them. Each photo keeps the license listed with it.</div></div></div><scri