 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Where are Airbnbs legal in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In the City of Myrtle Beach, only in the zones the city marks for them. Most neighborhoods of houses are zoned against any stay of less than 90 days. About three in four condos in the city are in a marked zone. North Myrtle Beach has no special zoning step for them, and Surfside Beach allows them in two districts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach a good place to buy a rental property?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For a yearly lease, the inland areas earn more rent for the price. A year's rent is about 9.1 percent of a house's price in Longs, against about 3.9 percent in Myrtle Beach. For a nightly rental, buy at the beach, where the rules for the address allow it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"North Myrtle Beach or Myrtle Beach for a rental?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For a nightly rental, North Myrtle Beach asks only for a license, the lodging taxes and its everyday rules. Myrtle Beach allows it only in marked zones, where most of its condos are. Nightly rentals took in more a year on average in North Myrtle Beach. The middle condo sold for about $300,000 in North Myrtle Beach and about $175,000 in Myrtle Beach."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Murrells Inlet in Horry or Georgetown County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Both. The county line runs through Murrells Inlet. The Census area of that name, which this page counts, lies in Georgetown County. Georgetown County requires no business license, and its resort district allows a house to be rented for stays of up to 30 days."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the property tax on a rental in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Outside the towns, most homes pay about $1,206 a year on each $100,000 of price at the rental rate, before fees. Inside the towns it is higher, and highest in Conway."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is the cheapest place to buy a rental near Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Conway for a house, at about $271,000 at the middle in the past year's recorded sales, and Little River for a condo, at about $155,000."}}]}</script>
