 The short answer
 You can buy a Grand Strand rental without visiting. A buyer in Canada has four extra steps . A local agent walks the property on video. A licensed home inspector reports on it. A South Carolina attorney runs the closing, and you sign the papers in your own state before a notary with two witnesses. Flood insurance starts on the day the loan closes. Property tax is charged at the 6 percent rate because the property is not your legal residence. Two things go wrong for remote buyers: wire fraud, and a signing package that does not meet South Carolina form. Both are avoidable.
